Source: ps3rsx
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), linux-headers-@KERNEL_RELEASE@
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3rsx-modules-@KERNEL_RELEASE@
Architecture: ppc64
Depends: linux-image-@KERNEL_RELEASE@ | ps3-kernel-@KERNEL_RELEASE@, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: ps3rsx-modules
Conflicts: ps3rsx-@KERNEL_RELEASE@
Replaces: ps3rsx-@KERNEL_RELEASE@
Description: DRM driver for the PS3's RSX GPU, for Linux @KERNEL_RELEASE@
 ps3rsx drives the RSX (an NV47) through the hypervisor and registers as nouveau, so Mesa's
 nv30 driver and Xorg's modesetting driver use it; loaded at boot. Also the RSX probe modules
 (rsx_ctx_probe, rsx_ctx_probe2, ps3fb_share_test) in extra/, loaded only by hand.

Package: ps3rsx-modules-@KERNEL_FLAVOUR@
Architecture: ppc64
Depends: ps3rsx-modules-@KERNEL_RELEASE@ (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: DRM driver for the PS3's RSX GPU (for the current @KERNEL_FLAVOUR@ kernel)
 This meta package depends on the ps3rsx modules for the current @KERNEL_FLAVOUR@ kernel, so upgrades
 bring in the modules for each new kernel.
